WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.486
Under and on top.

2
00:00:01.646 --> 00:00:07.637
See-through things go under: a watery wash, a light pencil line, a wax crayon that has to stay white.

3
00:00:07.797 --> 00:00:11.605
Covering things go on top: pen, thick paint, stuck paper.

4
00:00:11.765 --> 00:00:15.062
Get the order wrong and the layer underneath is lost.

5
00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:16.737
Dry first.

6
00:00:16.897 --> 00:00:18.755
The one rule that saves a picture.

7
00:00:18.915 --> 00:00:21.887
Pen on wet paint smears grey and tears the paper.

8
00:00:22.047 --> 00:00:24.090
Paint over wet paint goes muddy.

9
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.387
Every layer waits for the one below it.

10
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:29.130
What pen can do that paint cannot.

11
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:39.228
Thin, sharp, repeated marks: dots that build a texture, called stippling; a hard edge across a soft wash; grass, branches, wire, rain.

12
00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:42.267
That is why a painting gets pen marks on top.

13
00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:44.268
One layer too many.

14
00:00:44.428 --> 00:00:46.332
Adding is not always improving.

15
00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:49.650
Ask what the picture is missing, add that, and stop.

16
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.943
If a layer buries the thing the picture is about, take it back to the edges.
